Subject: [#94-10-179] Challenge to uploaders

One thing has always bothered me about the uploading idea.  From what I
understand, the idea is that some fab computer of the future will run a
simulation of your total brain/mental structure, thereby bringing you to
consciousness in and among the computer chips (or their successors).  My
problem is that simulations normally don't produce the physical attributes of
the things simulated: a simulation of a hurricane, for example, isn't wet
inside the computer; there's no rain and/or wind in there.  So how do you
know that your simulated mental structures will give rise to consciousness,
or anything like it?  

